# Dolphin right-click: add a Windows game or installer to Steam as a non-Steam
# shortcut, pinned to Proton. Pairs with the CDEmu menu beside it — mount a
# bin/cue, browse the disc, right-click the installer.
#
# inode/directory is deliberately NOT in the MimeType list, even though
# steam-add-game handles a directory perfectly well by reading autorun.inf. KIO
# matches on mimetype alone, so there is no way to offer the action on a mounted
# disc without also offering it on every other folder on the machine — and with
# no working submenu to nest it in (see below) that is two stray entries in
# every folder's context menu. The directory form stays available from a
# terminal: `steam-add-game /run/media/$USER/SOME_DISC`.
#
# It is also the better target in practice: autorun.inf routinely points at a
# menu shell rather than the installer, as on the BF1942 discs where it names
# AUTORUN.EXE and the thing you actually want is Setup.exe.
#
# Run inside kitty rather than detached: unlike cdemu-mount this is a
# conversation, not a fire-and-forget action. It prints the appid it derived and
# the next step, and its two most common outcomes — "several executables found,
# name one" and "Steam is running" — are text you have to read. --hold keeps the
# window up after it exits so the output survives. kitty specifically because
# this repo's provisioning guarantees it on every Linux host (see PACKAGES in
# run_onchange_provision-linux-host.sh.tmpl).
# X-KDE-Submenu is deliberately absent, and must stay absent. Plasma 6.7's
# KIO honours the key by filing the entry into a submenu list that
# KFileItemActions then never renders — the entry does not appear anywhere at
# all, with no warning and nothing in the logs. X-KDE-Show-In-Submenu is the
# key KIO 6.29 actually reads, but for *plugin* actions rather than service
# menus, so setting it merely stops the suppression; the actions still render
# flat. There is no working way to group service-menu actions under a heading
# on this Plasma version, so both actions sit directly in the context menu.
#
# Verified by building a KFileItemActions probe against libKF6KIOWidgets and
# asking KIO what it would offer for a given file, rather than by right-clicking
# and guessing — see docs/ if that harness is ever needed again.
#
# Type is not checked by KIO at all for files in this directory (Application and
# Service behave identically), and NoDisplay is not consulted either. Type=
# Application is the current documented form. NoDisplay is unnecessary regardless:
# the application launcher only scans applications/ directories, never
# kio/servicemenus, so a service menu was never at risk of appearing there.
#
# Autorun.exe and Setup.exe on one disc can carry different mimetypes
# (application/x-msdownload and application/vnd.microsoft.portable-executable
# respectively on the BF1942 discs), so the list below covers the PE spellings
# rather than assuming one.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Steam
Icon=steam
MimeType=application/vnd.microsoft.portable-executable;application/x-ms-dos-executable;application/x-msdownload;application/x-dosexec;application/x-msi;
Actions=steamAdd;steamPreview;

[Desktop Action steamAdd]
Name=Add to Steam (Proton)
Icon=steam
Exec=kitty --hold -e {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin/steam-add-game %f

[Desktop Action steamPreview]
Name=Preview what would be added
Icon=dialog-information
Exec=kitty --hold -e {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin/steam-add-game --dry-run %f
